# This app has two components, each with its own environment file -- there
# is no single combined .env that Django or Next.js reads directly. This
# file is an index, not something you copy and fill in.
#
#   backend/.env.example              -- local development (Django)
#   frontend/.env.example             -- local development (Next.js)
#   deploy/env-templates/backend.env.production   -- production (Django)
#   deploy/env-templates/frontend.env.production  -- production (Next.js)
#
# See docs/21_ENVIRONMENT_CONFIGURATION.md for what each variable does, and
# docs/DEPLOYMENT.md for how the production templates get onto the server.
#
# Rules, everywhere:
#   - Never commit a real .env file -- only .env.example / *.env.production
#     templates (with placeholder secrets) are checked into git.
#   - Every secret (Django secret key, JWT signing key, database password)
#     comes from the environment, never a literal in source.
